# Austin Ambassador five-door hatchback, 1982-1984.
#
# The facelifted Austin Princess: a five-door hatchback with a new front end,
# twin rectangular headlamps, a slatted grille and a tailgate. It is not a
# Princess: the Princess is a four-door saloon with concealed wipers, a taller
# bonnet line and a different grille and lamps, and only the front door skins
# are shared. The Princess is already in the tree.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin_Ambassador
#
# Dimensions 4.550 x 1.760 x 1.400 m, wheelbase 2.670 m.
#
# Shape reference: the nearest available to a side elevation is about 15 degrees
# ahead of broadside, both wheels visible. The flank is reconciled against the
# front and rear three-quarters and the head-on detail within the published
# dimensions. The limitation is recorded. The Commons title claiming a 1973
# first registration is wrong; the car carries a Y-suffix plate.
#
# Colours: grade (d), no UK document found. Black, Red, White and Blue are plain
# colour names, not claimed as factory names. Weights 6, 5, 5, 4, total 20,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 160 km/h. Comfort 70/435, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 70. Classes 2,3.
# Dates March 1982 to March 1984 production, road tail staggered 1998-2000.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/austin-ambassador.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/austin-ambassador.dae. References:
# citycars/references/austin-ambassador/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nearest side image is about 15 degrees ahead of
# broadside, so the flank was reconciled against the front and rear
# three-quarters and the head-on detail within the published dimensions. Grille,
# lamp and badge detail is simplified at sprite scale. The Ambassador front end
# and tailgate are modelled; it is not a Princess.


